{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a struct an event. It adds the "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance, the event’s name, consent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"category and schema version when you give them, a "},{"code":"schema","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" describing each stored property in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration order, and "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Decodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances that write each stored property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under its name. "},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declares rules a plain "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", number or array can’t carry, such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a minimum length or a pattern; the macro checks each keyword as it expands, and a tracker rejects an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event whose property breaks one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" includes this module. It re-exports "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Events"},{"type":"text","text":", so a file that imports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":" alone can expand the macro too. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol’s documentation, in that module,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shows the conformance written by hand; any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance, Swift’s synthesized one included,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is one a store can write. To export the schemas as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a JSON Schema tracking plan, pass them to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"search_performed\", consent: .functional, version: 2)","struct SearchPerformed {","    @Constrained(.minLength(1), .maxLength(200))","    var query: String","    var resultCount: Int","    var filter: String?","}","","let names = SearchPerformed.schema.properties.map(\\.name)  \/\/ [\"query\", \"resultCount\", \"filter\"]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Raise "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version:"},{"type":"text","text":" only for a change that records stored at the earlier version can’t be read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through; a store drops those records rather than reading them as the new shape."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers both macros, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shows which changes need a new version."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances, name and schema from its struct declaration, and declare the constraints its properties satisfy."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Defining an event","identifiers":["doc:\/\/EventMac